
You are given two tables: teams and goals.
   ⦿ The teams table contains information about teams.
   ⦿ The goals table records each goal scored by a team along with the time (in seconds) when the goal was scored.

• Write an SQL query to calculate the number of goals scored within the first 30 seconds by each team.

Output Requirements :
=====================

Display the following columns:
   ⦿ team → team name
   ⦿ goals_within_30_secs → number of goals scored within 30 seconds

Sort the results by:
   ⦿ Highest goal count first (descending order)
   ⦿ If two teams have the same goal count, then sort them alphabetically by team name


SQL query:
==========
    SELECT t.team_name AS team,
       COUNT(*) AS goals_within_30_secs
    FROM teams t
    JOIN goals g
    ON t.team_id = g.team_id
    WHERE g.goal_time <= 30
    GROUP BY t.team_name
    ORDER BY goals_within_30_secs DESC, t.team_name ASC;